## Review Summary

**7 files changed, −24 lines added, +48 lines removed**

### DRY Violations Fixed

| Issue | Location | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `SECS_PER_HOUR/DAY/WEEK/MONTH/YEAR` duplicated | `access_profile.rs` vs `util.rs` | Centralized in `util.rs`; `access_profile.rs` uses a private `time` submodule (preserves `i64` without forcing `AccessProfile` fields to `u64` — critical for postcard binary format compatibility) |
| `default_visibility()` triplicated | `entry.rs`, `chunk.rs`, `mcp/types.rs` | Single `pub(crate)` definition in `chunk.rs`; `entry.rs` imports it; `mcp/types.rs` serde attrs use `crate::chunk::default_visibility` |
| `SearchResult` duplicated (shadowed `store::SearchResult`) | `commands/mod.rs` vs `search/mod.rs` | Removed local struct from `commands/mod.rs`; `commands/search.rs` now returns `Vec<crate::HierarchicalSearchResult>` directly (identical fields, eliminates unnecessary wrapper type) |

### Key Design Decisions

- **`access_profile.rs` time submodule**: Kept as `i64` because `AccessProfile`'s `created_at`/`last_rolled` fields are `i64` (already serialized as such by postcard). Changing those fields to `u64` would break existing blob store binaries. The private submodule documents intent while keeping the values in sync with `util.rs`.
- **`commands::SearchResult` removal**: Turns out it wasn't truly dead — `commands/search.rs` was using it as a wrapper. The cleaner fix was to use `crate::HierarchicalSearchResult` directly, which has the same fields and was already part of the public API.

### Quality Gates
- ✅ `cargo build --features full`
- ✅ `cargo clippy --features full -- -D warnings`
- ✅ `cargo fmt --check`
- ✅ `cargo test --features full` (all unit tests pass; 8 integration tests correctly ignored — require local Ollama)
- ⚠️ `num-bigint-dig v0.8.4` future incompatibility (transitive dep, filed separately)
